.TH LINEFIX 1 "August 2026" "linefix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linefix \- convert text-file line endings safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linefix
.B lf
.I file
.br
.B linefix
.B crlf
.I file
.br
.B linefix
.B check
.I file
.br
.B linefix
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B linefix
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linefix
is a small, dependency-free utility for converting text files between LF and
CRLF line endings. It modifies files in place, preserves permission bits and
trailing-newline state, and does not rewrite files that already use the
requested format.
.PP
Before processing a file,
.B linefix
checks for NUL bytes and an unusually high proportion of control bytes.
Likely binary input is refused instead of modified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "lf " file
Convert each CRLF sequence (\er\en) to LF (\en).
.TP
.BI "crlf " file
Convert LF sequences to CRLF. Existing CRLF sequences are normalized first,
preventing accidental \er\er\en sequences.
.TP
.BI "check " file
Inspect the file without modifying it and print one of
.BR LF ,
.BR CRLF ,
.BR Mixed ,
or
.BR "No line endings" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command usage, examples, and a summary of safety behavior, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program name and build version, then exit.
.SH CHECK OUTPUT
.TP
.B LF
All detected line endings are LF.
.TP
.B CRLF
All detected line endings are CRLF.
.TP
.B Mixed
Both LF and CRLF endings are present.
.TP
.B No line endings
The file is empty or contains no LF or CRLF ending.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be read, checked, converted, or safely replaced.
.TP
.B 2
The command-line arguments were invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the line endings used by a file:
.PP
.RS
.B linefix check README.md
.RE
.PP
Normalize a shell script to LF:
.PP
.RS
.B linefix lf script.sh
.RE
.PP
Normalize a text file to CRLF:
.PP
.RS
.B linefix crlf notes.txt
.RE
.SH NOTES
Bare carriage returns are preserved and are not treated as line endings.
An empty file and a file without a newline are valid inputs and remain
unchanged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/linefix
Default executable location used by the Unix installer.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/linefix.1
Default manual-page location used by the Unix installer.
